# Trivy exceptions for THIRD-PARTY images KubeBolt bundles but does not build.
#
# Used ONLY by the two `preflight-third-party-scan` steps in
# .github/workflows/release.yml (victoria-metrics and vmagent). KubeBolt's own
# images — api, web, single-container — are scanned by `image-scan` against the strict
# `.trivyignore`, which stays empty of entries.
#
# The split exists because the two cases are not the same problem. When a CVE
# lands in a dependency we compile, the answer is to bump and rebuild, and the
# gate should keep failing until we do. When it lands inside a vendor's published
# binary, we cannot fix it — only wait for their rebuild or drop the dependency.
# One shared file would let the second silence the first.
#
# Every entry still needs an owner, a justification, and a remove-by date, and
# the same rule applies: this is not a way to push an urgent release out.
#
# Format:
#   CVE-YYYY-NNNNN  # YYYY-MM-DD <owner> — justification + remove-by date

# No entries. The Go stdlib waivers for victoria-metrics / vmagent
# v1.148.0-scratch (8 CVEs, remove-by 2026-09-15) were closed on 2026-09-28 by
# moving the pin to v1.153.0-scratch, built on Go 1.27.1: Trivy reports 0
# CRITICAL/HIGH on both images. The pin lives in deploy/helm/kubebolt/values.yaml,
# deploy/docker-compose.yml and the kubebolt-agent chart (vmagent); bump them
# together — the preflight fails on drift.
#
# 2026-10-09: v1.153.0-scratch picked up CVE-2026-78667 (net/http) and
# CVE-2026-97031 (crypto/tls), fixed in Go 1.27.2 — no stable VictoriaMetrics
# release carried the fix yet. Moved to v1.154.0-rc0-scratch (0 CRITICAL/HIGH
# on both images; rules, queries, remote_write/import/export and vmagent
# scraping checked against it). A release candidate does not ship: move to the
# v1.154.0 final before cutting a release — or, if it is late, cut the release
# on v1.153.0-scratch with those two CVEs waived here.
#
# 2026-10-12: 2.3.1 was cut that way, on v1.153.0-scratch with three CVEs waived
# (CVE-2026-78667, CVE-2026-78669 — HTTP/2 in Go and x/net v0.59.0 —, and
# CVE-2026-97031); see the v2.3.1 tag. Not needed here while the pin is rc0.
#
# 2026-10-13: 2.4.0 moves the pin to the v1.154.0-scratch final (released
